<strong><span><span><span><span>The Veil Orthodox</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy IPA with Citra, Citra Dynaboost, Nectaron, Nectaron Cryo, Citra Cryo &amp; Enigma<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Vasen West Coast Savage</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> West Coast TIPA with Amarillo, Nectaron, Chinook &amp; Centennial<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Ballad Black Lager</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Schwarzbier</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/d9179b9d-ffe6-6ace-29d3-71ef008d35bf.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f966/32.png\" alt=\"🥦\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"> OK you've been asking for both of these</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Other Half Space Broccoli</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> DDH DIPA with Mosaic, Simcoe, Hallertau Blanc &amp; Galaxy</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span>Starr Hill Christmas Ale</span></span></strong></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/acdbb97e-5246-6e12-8ab8-8d2d48f466a2.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f385/32.png\" alt=\"🎅\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"> </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Troegs </span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>favorite things are here</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span>Blizzard of Hops</span></span></strong><span><span> Winter IPA</span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span>Most Wonderful Beer of the Year </span></span></strong><span><span>Mixed Pack featuring Mad Elf, Naked Elf, Mad Dreams &amp; Chocolate Elf</span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/ef9c2cc3-baa1-621e-f58c-06c206fb2138.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f969/32.png\" alt=\"🥩\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"> Welcome to the shop </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Vander Provisions</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>! Wagyu beef sticks - no fillers, no added nitrites or nitrates, traditionally fermented, 100% Wagyu beef. Here in 2 flavors!</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Hardwood Smoked</span></span></span></strong></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Sweet &amp; Spicy</span></span></span></strong></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/05c86a99-9706-69e1-0369-d90556672f76.png\" width=\"229\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1fab6/32.png\" alt=\"🪶\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"> Fresh in from </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Hawkley</span></span></span></strong></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Superdelic Krush</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Hazy Session IPA&nbsp;with Superdelic &amp; Krush</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Fly By Night</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Dark Lager</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>*expected Friday*</span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/1cea0433-6a73-6515-9a2d-f135f473a9cc.jpeg\" width=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Le Mesnil Blanc de Blanc Grand Cru Brut Champagne</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>I'm not the only one in the wine business in my family - my BIL is a Sommelier in LA and my SIL is a Sommelier in Dallas. We love to chat wine and my SIL tipped me off to Le Mesnil Blanc de Blanc Champagne. Founded in 1937, Le Mesnil produces this Grand Cru Champagne on the chalk soils of the Cotes de Blancs. Le Mesnil has the classic Champagne sniff - brioche and fresh baked bread - followed by citrus, creaminess and decadent bubbles.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Bottex Vin du Bugey Cru Cerdon Savoie</span></span><span><span>:</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>My \"yoga\" friends and I usually skip the mimosas and go straight for a bottle of Bugey. Located equidistant between Geneva and Lyon, on the approach to the Alps, Bugey is one of France’s best kept wine secrets. Produced in the “methode ancestrale” sparkling style and pouring a delightful ruby in color, Bottex Bugey has whiffs of cherries and cranberries followed by notes of strawberries and a touch of natural sweetness.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span>Les Lunes Cosmic Blend </span><span>: </span></strong><span><span><span><span>Another gorgeous chillable red from Les Lunes, Cosmic Blend is the brooding big brother to the Astral Blend that previously graced our shelves. A touch more blue in fruit presentation - think blueberry, crunchy blackcurrant - but with all the complex herbal and spice notes, plush texture, and zippy acidity that you've come to expect from Les Lunes. Incredibly drinkable, this is the bottle to convince any of your skeptic friends of the beauty of natural wine. Organic, dry-farmed, native yeast, unfined/unfiltered.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/94a85b9e-47f5-17a7-4b9d-502748cf2750.jpeg\" width=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span>Those of you who have been coming to The Brew Shop for a while (or maybe even those that just discovered us) know that I love a good rant. I've got rants about a myriad of topics, including margarine, stoplight coordination, college football, socks, gym equipment, and of course some more serious topics, like what the movie Sideways did to Merlot. <br></span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>For those unfamiliar, the movie Sideways came out in 2004 and includes one famous line from the film's main character Miles, played by Paul Giamatti, in which he exclaims \"If anyone orders Merlot, I'm leaving. I'm not drinking any fucking Merlot!\" And with that, Merlot sales dropped. Truly. California Merlot sales saw an enormous drop, which led to CA wineries ripping out Merlot vines in favor of Pinot Noir, a wine Sideways glamorized. I won't get into my full rant, but suffice it to say I find people running away from Merlot because of a taken-out-of-context line from a movie (Miles hated Merlot because it was his ex-wife's favorite, not for reasons related to the wine or grape itself) to be absurd.<br></span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>Well fast forward 20+ years and the wine industry is ready to say \"The Sideways Effect\" seems to have finally run its course. California Merlot plantings and sales are up, and a new generation of drinkers who are unfamiliar with the movie Sideways are letting this beautiful wine speak for itself. (Let the record show that my old ass has been a fan of Merlot this entire time.) All that is to say, I was very excited to see</span></span></span><strong><span><span><span> Alias Merlot</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> hit our shelves. </span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>Alias Merlot comes from Northern California and is brought to you by the Folktale Wine Group. One of my favorite things about this wine is that it's made in a cave. (I do have a very positive and enthusiastic rant about caves as well.) This underground cave helps regulate the humidity and temperature to create a more consistent wine year-over-year. </span><span>Alias hits all the CA Merlot notes you want to see: dark berries, earth, baking spice, and a touch of smoke. Pillowy tannins pair with a velvety texture in a medium body, wrapped in a finish that's easy and straightforward. A lovely red, and at $14.99, I'm happy to drink fucking Merlot any day of the week.</span></span></span></p>\n<p><em><span><span><span><span>This week’s writeup is brought to you by Julie</span></span></span></span></em></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/d9fbdb97-b413-ec30-bc34-336ee4155d1b.png\" width=\"612\" alt=\"breathe11x17in_1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>Thanks for your business! See you soon, Beth, Julie &amp; Aidan and the entire Brew Crew</p>",
